WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.767
-My next guest
is one of the stars

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.834
of the blockbuster television
show "Stranger Things."

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.734
He's also the host
of the series "Prank Encounters"

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:11.434
with Season 2 now
streaming on Netflix.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:14.400
Please welcome Gaten Matarazzo!

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.934
-♪ Gaten Matarazzo,
bet you didn't know ♪

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.834
♪ That the name Gaten
is short for Gaetano ♪

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:26.667
♪ Gaten Matarazzo,
be careful what you do ♪

00:00:26.667 --> 00:00:27.834
-Thank you, bud!

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.200
Always come through for me.
-Thank you.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.701
It's always such a pleasure
to be here.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.033
-I always love seeing you, pal.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.100
We have a lot
to get into, buddy.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.300
You got a job...
-I did.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.834
-...during the pandemic,
and not an acting job.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.133
-Not an acting job, no.

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.801
-You got a job at a restaurant.

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.267
-Yeah.
-Explain this to me,

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.501
and why did you do that?

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:48.567
-So, well, over the summer
during the pandemic,

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.234
there were a couple
of restaurants

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.067
near where I live in New Jersey

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.300
that were open because
they all had outdoor seating.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.067
And so, both of my siblings
got a job at this place,

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.767
a couple of my friends did,
some of my cousins,

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.734
so everybody I've ever
hanged out with --

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:04.834
everybody I've ever known
and met and talked to.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:07.868
And I was sitting
on the couch one day,

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.567
and my brother was like,
"Going to work.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:11.934
I'll see you at like 11:00."
I was like, "Okay."

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:15.100
And he leaves,
and I'm playing "Mario Kart"

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.701
and I'm still playing
"Mario Kart."

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.534
-Yeah.
-And then after a while,

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:20.801
I'm still playing "Mario Kart."

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:24.400
And so, I got really good at it

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.567
to the point which was just --
I knew it was sad.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.501
I'm like, "Wow, I'm good.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.868
I need to stop."
-I got to stop, yeah.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.834
-And so I was like,
if they're all leaving

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.701
and they're the only people I
know, I might just follow them,

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.968
might just go with them,
and so I did.

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:40.567
-So you got a job
at this restaurant?

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.701
And what did you do?
-I was a food runner.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.200
I literally --
I stood at the line,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.667
and then, when orders were up,
I just brought them to tables.

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.167
-And did people freak out?

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.901
-Sometimes, yeah,
which is pretty fun.

00:01:51.901 --> 00:01:53.334
-"Gaten Matar--
What's going on?"

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.033
-Well, I had, like, a disguise.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.400
I was, like, incognito,
which was fun.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.667
I had, like,
the restaurant shirt on.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.067
I had a hat that was
for the restaurant.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.868
I got to tuck
all my hair into it.

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.434
And I had one
of the sleeve masks,

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:06.968
the one you pull
over your whole face.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:10.300
And I just tucked that into
the hat, so just my eyes --

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.400
It was just my eyes,
and people still recognized --

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.234
I would go to tables
and, like, drop food

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.834
and be like [Deep voice]
"There you go. Enjoy."

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.634
[ Normal voice ] I wouldn't even
let them hear my voice.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:22.434
And people would just look at me
for a second, squint like that,

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.467
and be like,
"Are you Gaten Matarazzo?"

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.167
So, 3-year-olds,
like, toddler people.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.734
-Wait, 3 --
-Yeah.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.968
-I'm so sorry. 3-year-olds...

00:02:31.968 --> 00:02:33.667
-Yeah.
-...follow you?

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.601
-There are, like, toddlers
who love "Stranger Things,"

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.767
who are just -- Yeah, they think
it's like the bomb.com.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.133
-But it's a little scary.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.167
-It's a little scary.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.467
-Yeah, for a 3-year-old.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:47.734
-Sometimes it's like, people who
don't speak most words

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.701
will look at me
and just be like, "Dustin."

00:02:49.701 --> 00:02:51.067
I'm like --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.234
-Like, wow, that's your
first word, is Dustin.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.567
-There it is.
It's great. It's really cool.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:59.300
-'Cause I get scared.
I'm way old.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.834
And -- But let's talk about
"Stranger Things,"

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:04.033
'cause you were
shooting Season 4.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.267
Then, obviously, COVID.
You shut down.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:09.067
Are you getting back?
Are you back?

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.167
-We're getting back.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:12.234
-But you told me
that this season

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.534
that you know of
that you've shot so far,

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.868
you told me it might be
the scariest one.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:18.000
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.767
That's the one thing
that I've noticed.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.300
I was reading it, I'm like,

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.067
"They're going for it this year.
That's pretty cool."

00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:24.567
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:28.000
So I don't know if the toddlers
are going to enjoy it as much

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.701
this time going around.
-Yeah, okay, alright, so, yeah.

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:31.167
But maybe, you know -- Yeah.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:32.634
Maybe you would
release it in segments.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:34.901
By the time they get to see it,
they'll be 4 or 5 years old.

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:36.167
-Yeah! I think it'd be great.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.968
At the rate we're going,
they might be like 12.

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.434
-Yeah, perfect, alright, good.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.467
I want to talk about
this show on Netflix

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:43.200
that you executive-produced.
-Please.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.367
-"Prank Encounters."
-"Prank Encounters."

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:48.100
-I remember a show growing up
called "Candid Camera."

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.234
-Ooh.
-And it was a fun show.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:51.334
It was family-friendly.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.334
It's, like, an old woman
would be sweeping.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.367
Then you'd walk by, and she'd,
like, tap you on the butt,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:56.434
and you're like, that happened?

00:03:56.434 --> 00:03:57.667
People would laugh,
and it's great.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.934
-It's great.
-What you do...

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.567
-Is not like that.
-No.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.734
No, it's scary,

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:06.300
and it's hilarious
to watch people's reactions

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.667
getting scared.
-It is.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.934
-Do you get scared, in a way,

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:13.200
that people might
hit you or something?

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.033
-Every time I get up and know
I have a prank later that day.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:19.267
They take sometimes two, three
hours to film the whole thing.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.534
So you're waiting there
for a while,

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.801
and then you go in
for like a two-minute reveal,

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.667
which is like 30 seconds
of, "That's cool,"

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:29.033
and 30 seconds of, "Dude, please
don't deck me in the head."

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:32.467
Because I'm so scared,
'cause I think if I get punched,

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.234
I don't really have a defense.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.300
I kind of deserve it
at that point.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:38.167
-No, no.
-Well, if I'm scaring

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:40.100
the actual crap
out of like a bunch of people,

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.501
which I've done a bunch
on this show,

00:04:42.501 --> 00:04:44.300
if I were to go in there
and just [Pops lips]

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.701
I'd be like, "Fair."
-"Yeah, I saw that one coming."

00:04:46.701 --> 00:04:49.434
But, I mean, dude, what are
people's most common reaction

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:52.267
when -- 'Cause I've seen
a few episodes,

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.634
and there's giant reactions.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:57.133
-Mm. Usually,
the reveal is great.

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.133
It's big. It's lively.
But throughout the prank --

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:03.067
We condense them down to like
20-minute, half-hour episodes

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.133
but of like a three-hour prank.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:06.701
You're getting the highlights
pretty much,

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.434
because it's a lot
of waiting around,

00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:10.968
especially because we prank
two people in one prank.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.200
That's what we do.
We get two people.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.167
We see how they interact
with each other

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:17.801
while the actors around them
are as useless as possible

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.334
to a really scary situation.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:21.868
We like to see if they step up
and try to be leaders,

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:24.267
and usually, they do,
which is really cool.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.434
And I think it says something.

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:27.000
Yeah, usually,
if there's no other options,

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.934
people will step up,
and I think that's really cool.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.200
-That's right.
-But for the majority

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.234
of the time, it's like --
They're like,

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.834
"If I don't move,
they won't see me."

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.767
-[ Laughs ]
-And we don't want that!

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:39.300
Like, that's not fun to watch.
You want someone to move around,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.367
and you want somebody
to interact.

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:41.901
And so that's
the biggest challenge

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.033
for a lot of our actors,
who are incredible,

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.701
incredible improv actors
who work on the show.

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:47.601
-Very funny.
I want to show a clip.

00:05:47.601 --> 00:05:51.033
Here is Gaten Matarazzo in
Season 2 of "Prank Encounters."

00:05:51.033 --> 00:05:52.200
Take a look at this.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.667
-Okay.

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.501
Okay.

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.067
Mr. Timms?

00:05:57.167 --> 00:05:59.801
Mr. Timms?

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:01.067
-[ Groans, gasps ]

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:02.100
-Aah!

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.501
-[ Grunting ]

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:06.968
-Oh, my God.
Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:06:06.968 --> 00:06:08.801
-[ Hissing ]

00:06:08.801 --> 00:06:12.767
Aah!
-[ Screaming ]

00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:16.167
-[ Hisses ]
-Bennett!

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:18.400
Wait, Bennett!

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.434
Come back!

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:21.934
Bennett!

00:06:21.934 --> 00:06:24.100
-Oh, he's making a run for it.
He's making a run for it.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.767
We have a runner.
We have a runner.

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:28.200
-[ Hisses ]

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.634 --> 00:06:30.834
-Yeah.

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:33.000
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.300
-Oh, he just took off.
It's fantastic.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.300
-It's amazing.
-Gaten Matarazzo, everybody!

